id: core/memory-update
title: "memory update"
kind: core
status: v1
updated: 2026-07-21

definition: >
  A memory update is an authorized event reduction that changes the map after
  a bounded move meets proof, fails proof, or reveals a new lacuna. Attributed
  reports, corrections, desires, consent, choices, and permissions may also be
  recorded without pretending they are empirical proof.

friendly_label: memory
technical_mechanism: replay

records:
  before: "what the map held before movement"
  after: "what the map can hold after proof"
  changed: []
  new_lacuna: []

rule: >
  Memory should update from proof and replay, not from intensity, resonance,
  coincidence, or AI confidence.

boundary:
  - "Memory is not objective record."
  - "Replay is not proof unless tied to evidence."
  - "Only authorized events update canonical materialized state."
  - "Only suitable evidence or proof upgrades empirical claims."
  - "Presentation-only events never alter semantic meaning."

proof:
  source:
    - interface/memory.yawn
    - core/proof-and-boundary.yawn
    - 05-proof/replay.ion
  status: seed-backed
